
This directory is intended for PlatformIO Test Runner and project tests.

Unit Testing is a software testing method by which individual units of
source code, sets of one or more MCU program modules together with associated
control data, usage procedures, and operating procedures, are tested to
determine whether they are fit for use. Unit testing finds problems early
in the development cycle.

More information about PlatformIO Unit Testing:
- https://docs.platformio.org/en/latest/advanced/unit-testing/index.html

Desktop logging checks (no board required):

    python -m unittest discover -s test -p "test_*.py" -v

For C++ checks, use a Visual Studio Developer Command Prompt from the project
root. Create .pio\log_v4_validation, then compile and run each test:

    cl /nologo /EHsc /std:c++14 /Itest\fakes\logging /Iinclude test\log_record_test.cpp /Fe.pio\log_v4_validation\log_record_test.exe /Fo.pio\log_v4_validation\log_record_test.obj
    .pio\log_v4_validation\log_record_test.exe
    cl /nologo /EHsc /std:c++14 /Itest\fakes\logging /Iinclude test\closed_loop_logging_test.cpp /Fe.pio\log_v4_validation\closed_loop_logging_test.exe /Fo.pio\log_v4_validation\closed_loop_logging_test.obj
    .pio\log_v4_validation\closed_loop_logging_test.exe
    cl /nologo /EHsc /std:c++14 /Iinclude test\pid_test.cpp /Fe.pio\log_v4_validation\pid_test.exe /Fo.pio\log_v4_validation\pid_test.obj
    .pio\log_v4_validation\pid_test.exe

These check the real binary writer, pressure-sample reuse, PID snapshots,
closed-loop PT3 feedback, clipping flags, and PID state behavior. Logging fakes
are isolated under test\fakes\logging; they do not control physical hardware.
